# Domain

- Do not import frameworks, transports, databases, renderers, or vendor SDKs.
- Model IDs and constrained values with branded or opaque types.
- Represent state variants and errors with discriminated unions.
- Implement behavior as pure functions returning immutable state, events, or typed errors.
- Inject clock, ID generation, ruleset behavior, and external lookups through narrow ports.
- Keep aggregates small and enforce invariants at their mutation boundary.
- Name domain events as past-tense facts and include schema versions.
- Access other modules only through their public contracts.
- Keep VTT-neutral concepts free of game-system-specific fields.
- Write table-driven and property tests without I/O or wall-clock dependencies.
